/**
 * Finds the optimal position within a given text segment to wrap a line,
 * respecting a maximum line width. This method prioritizes breaking lines
 * at explicit newline/tab characters, then at whitespace characters (space,
 * carriage return), and finally, if no natural break is found, it will
 * chop the line at the maximum allowed width.
 *
 * The method assumes `width` represents the maximum number of characters
 * allowed on the current line segment, starting from `startPos`.
 *
 * @param text The complete string to be wrapped. Must not be null.
 * @param width The maximum desired length of the line segment. Must be a positive integer.
 * @param startPos The starting index in the `text` from which to consider the current line segment.
 *                 Must be a valid index within the `text` string (0 to text.length()).
 * @return The index in the `text` string where the current line should end and the next line should begin.
 *         This index will be the first character of the next line.
 *         Returns -1 if no further wrapping is needed for the remainder of the text
 *         (i.e., the segment from `startPos` to the end of `text` fits within `width`).
 * @throws IllegalArgumentException if `text` is null or `width` is not positive.
 * @throws IndexOutOfBoundsException if `startPos` is out of bounds for the `text` string.
 */
