/**
 * Skips the next value in the JSON stream. If the current token is a {@link JsonToken#NAME},
 * this method first consumes the name and then skips its associated value. If the current
 * token is a primitive value (string, number, boolean, null), it consumes that value.
 * If the current token is the beginning of an array ({@link JsonToken#BEGIN_ARRAY}) or
 * an object ({@link JsonToken#BEGIN_OBJECT}), this method recursively consumes all
 * tokens within that array or object, effectively skipping the entire structure.
 * After skipping, the internal path index for the current level is incremented.
 *
 * @throws IOException if an I/O error occurs during parsing, or if the end of the
 *                     JSON document is reached unexpectedly while skipping.
 * @throws AssertionError if an unexpected JSON token is encountered, indicating
 *                        a potential issue with the internal state or the JSON structure.
 */
