                + " at line " + getLineNumber() + " column " + getColumnNumber() + " path " + getPath());
        }
        peeked = PEEKED_NONE;
        pathIndices[stackSize - 1]++;
        return result;
    }

    if (p == PEEKED_NUMBER) {
        // For PEEKED_NUMBER, the value is already buffered.
        // We need to parse it as an integer.
        // If it contains a decimal point, it's not a valid integer for this method.
        // We can try parsing as long first to avoid double precision issues for large integers.
        try {
            // Attempt to parse as long first to handle larger integer values
            // and then check if it fits into int.
            long longValue = Long.parseLong(new String(buffer, pos, peekedNumberLength));
            result = (int) longValue;
            if (longValue != result) { // Check for overflow/underflow when casting to int
                throw new NumberFormatException("Expected an int but was " + new String(buffer, pos, peekedNumberLength)
                    + " at line " + getLineNumber() + " column " + getColumnNumber() + " path " + getPath());
            }
            // Check if the number string contains a decimal point, which would make it not an integer.
            // This is a strict interpretation for nextInt().
            for (int i = 0; i < peekedNumberLength; i++) {
